### 6. Linguistic and sociological implications

The automated work is the search for recurring component relations under stated linguistic constraints. It makes a candidate mechanism explicit, counts its exact applicability, locates challenges, and checks whether a refinement survives repeated use. That is a substantial part of moving from individually analyzed senses to a systematic account of a lexical field. It also gives small numbers of direct judgments a measurable downstream effect. One question can alter which questions are worth asking next.

A sociology of this work could trace where interpretive effort and authority move as propagation becomes cheap. The natural units of observation are hours spent defining scopes, analyzing contrast cases, or reviewing warrants, as well as direct and propagated assignments. Source inventories and guard choices are part of that record. English dictionary and ontology categories can determine which senses are easy to collect, compare, and generalize over. A cross-linguistic extension would need local sources, speaker-grounded checks, and explicit analysis of how the proposed explication travels across languages. [Levisen, Fernández, and Hein 2022](https://doi.org/10.7146/sss.v13i1.135133)

The present evidence concerns mostly measurement senses, a fixed proposal vocabulary, and same-model audits on withheld definitions. In the final closure snapshot, Wiktionary accounted for 13,616,617 unresolved coordinates and WordNet for 8,454,003. The trial exercised WordNet scopes, so broader source coverage is a separate empirical question. Corpus replay establishes reproducibility and consistency under the recorded evidence. Independent human semantic judgments would test the warrants and resulting signs. A study of wider applicability would hold out whole lexical families and sources, separately report justified, abstained, and wrong judgments by class, and measure review time. This design would test whether gains survive more heterogeneous meanings and whether they save the interpretive work that matters to linguists.

Definition coverage and runtime sense selection also require separate measurements. The refreshed candidate contains all 155,113 active definition identities and adds 246,483. On the shared identities, 229,339 assignments match, 2,905 previously open cells have values, and 704 previously assigned cells are open. There are zero direct changes between known values. The largest withdrawal group has 414 CAUSE cells and 269 HAPPEN cells associated with removed VerbNet assertions. [Snapshot coverage](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-coverage-comparison.json) · [Exact-identity comparison](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-domain-delta.json) · [Withdrawal provenance](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-reopen-provenance.json)

In a fixed sample of twelve sentences, the candidate preserved ambiguity for all 31 content tokens and emitted no signed lexical evidence for those tokens. The active snapshot emitted signs for three of 30 content tokens and failed one modal case that the candidate encoded. Neither an all-sense nor a part-of-speech-compatible consensus recovered a signed value in that sample. With an explicit definition identity, the candidate distinguished the anatomical heart's BODY domain of $\{+1\}$, GOOD domain of $\{0\}$, and open WANT domain. These observations separate storage fidelity, contextual sense resolution, and compatibility with the sentence encoder. [Sentence sample](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-sentence-compatibility.json) · [Consensus preview](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-consensus-preview.json)

The first sparse snapshot was published. Its isolated copy replayed all 401,596 records with complete support search and zero mismatches. The release audit confirmed 12 supplied values and recorded one abstention. It retained 280,661 explicit zeros and 22,083,473 open lexical coordinates. Contextual grounding now binds exact WordNet noun definitions when a native lexical witness supports the binding. In the fixed sample, it selected the riverbank sense and preserved ambiguity for the other 30 content tokens. The controls also selected the financial sense in the mortgage context. An initial type-only rule selected the person sense of *light* near *electrician*. This counterexample led to a required lexical witness, with type overlap used to distinguish competing witnesses or expose a disagreement. The corrected encoder abstains on that case. [Sparse publication](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-001-publication.json) · [Active runtime verification](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sparse-release-001-runtime-verification.json)

The word and sentence scales have different validation obligations. In the earlier build, “I waited for some time” and “I waited for a long time” produced identical event expressions. The approved mapping for *(for) some time* now denotes an interval of unspecified extent. Thirteen runtime checks covered the contrast with short and long duration, the distinction between event duration and an interval before or after another event, and preservation of attachment ambiguity. The refreshed catalogue has mappings for all 65 NSM units. Full replay checked 401,596 definition records with complete support search and zero mismatches. The 56-bank basis and every stored domain matched the preceding checkpoint. The release audit counted the exact duration chart record as sentence provenance, leaving 401,595 lexical definitions and 22,083,491 open lexical coordinates at this checkpoint. Publication remained blocked pending complete definitions, a validated prime foundation, and a release semantic audit. [Earlier contrast](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/foundation-duration-probe.json) · [Runtime checks](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sentence-duration-runtime-verification.json) · [Catalogue replay](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sentence-duration-catalog-verification.json) · [Release accounting](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-continuation/sentence-duration-release-accounting.json)

### Reproduction record

The frozen plan, source scope, model digest, and replay commands are versioned in the GSE workspace. Retain the candidate identities and the per-epoch selection, teaching, audit, admission, and replay reports with each update to the results ledger. [Broader trial plan](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-12-ssl-grounded-comparison/plan.json) · [Epoch runner](../../../../gse/scripts/run_lexicon_epochs.py)

The [semantic-molecule research record](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-13-ssl-explicit-genera/020-molecule-research-notes.md) preserves the complete-section NSM reading, inspected composition code and a separate 2,366-cell biological BODY opportunity. That screen is unadmitted, has made no model calls and is outside the frozen 020 release. Its next obligation is a defensible molecule-to-bank projection and informative direct teaching, rather than treating unobserved targets as confirmation.

